      "our_prose": "Cosmos is a sun-loving summer flower that cannot take any frost, so wait until the danger of frost has passed, and give our cool spring soil a little extra time to warm before setting it out. There is no local university planting guide made just for this flower here, so these dates come from the same warm-season facts used wherever cosmos is grown, adjusted to our region's frost dates. Expect one solid summer-into-fall bloom rather than the huge stands cosmos makes in hotter climates.",
